% String pins for entries carrying a caveat.
%
% A caveat tells the oracle not to fail on an entry, which is exactly the point:
% these entries genuinely disagree with SEL and the disagreement is declared. But
% it also means their semantics stop being checked against a server, and the
% string they emit becomes the only thing left holding them. That half was
% missing. Mutating ansi's LOWER to UPPER proved it: the oracle printed
% `caveat LOWER("ABC") SEL="abc" DB="ABC" [unicode-case]` and reported 0 differ,
% because LOWER already carried unicode-case for an honest reason and no case
% named LOWER on any dialect.
%
% php/bin/sqlt now requires one of these per caveated entry per target, traced
% rather than claimed. Each case here exists because that check asked for it.

### name: pin.mariadb.decode-base64
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
BLEN(DECODE_BASE64("aGk="))
--- expect
LENGTH(FROM_BASE64('aGk='))
===
### name: pin.mariadb.lower
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
LOWER("ABC")
--- expect
LOWER('ABC')
===
### name: pin.mariadb.max
--- dialect
mariadb
--- source
MAX(1, 2)
--- expect
GREATEST(1, 2)
===
### name: pin.postgresql.decode-base64
--- dialect
postgresql
--- source
BLEN(DECODE_BASE64("aGk="))
--- expect
octet_length(decode('aGk=', 'base64'))
===
### name: pin.postgresql.lower
--- dialect
postgresql
--- source
LOWER("ABC")
--- expect
lower(CAST('ABC' AS TEXT))
===
### name: pin.postgresql.power
--- dialect
postgresql
--- source
POWER(2, 10)
--- expect
power(CAST(2 AS NUMERIC), CAST(10 AS NUMERIC))
===
### name: pin.postgresql.rfind
--- dialect
postgresql
--- source
RFIND('b', "abc")
--- expect
regexp_instr(CAST('abc' AS TEXT) COLLATE "C", '(?s)b')
===
### name: pin.postgresql.rmatch
--- dialect
postgresql
--- source
RMATCH('^a', "abc")
--- expect
(CAST('abc' AS TEXT) COLLATE "C" ~ '(?s)^a')
===
### name: pin.sqlite.abs
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
ABS(-2.50)
--- expect
abs((-'2.50'))
===
### name: pin.sqlite.ceil
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
CEIL(1.2)
--- expect
ceil('1.2')
===
### name: pin.sqlite.floor
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
FLOOR(1.8)
--- expect
floor('1.8')
===
### name: pin.sqlite.max
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
MAX(1, 2)
--- expect
max('1', '2')
===
### name: pin.sqlite.power
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
POWER(2, 3)
--- expect
pow('2', '3')
===
### name: pin.sqlite.trunc
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
TRUNC(1.9)
--- expect
trunc('1.9')
===
### name: pin.sqlite.!=
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
1 != 2
--- expect
(CAST('1' AS NUMERIC) <> CAST('2' AS NUMERIC))
===
### name: pin.sqlite.*
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
2 * 3
--- expect
('2' * '3')
===
### name: pin.sqlite.-
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
5 - 2
--- expect
('5' - '2')
===
### name: pin.sqlite.<
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
1 < 2
--- expect
(CAST('1' AS NUMERIC) < CAST('2' AS NUMERIC))
===
### name: pin.sqlite.<=
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
1 <= 2
--- expect
(CAST('1' AS NUMERIC) <= CAST('2' AS NUMERIC))
===
### name: pin.sqlite.>
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
2 > 1
--- expect
(CAST('2' AS NUMERIC) > CAST('1' AS NUMERIC))
===
### name: pin.sqlite.>=
--- dialect
sqlite
--- source
2 >= 1
--- expect
(CAST('2' AS NUMERIC) >= CAST('1' AS NUMERIC))
===
